                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "651e9b4b-3418-4b30-b9ab-602c60718ef2",
                        "entry_id": "da3237bc-0adc-3025-8255-9611b3da52fb",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more tacitly"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8477a67a-a4af-491f-adc2-13d12088d39e",
                        "entry_id": "da3237bc-0adc-3025-8255-9611b3da52fb",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most tacitly"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                        "entry_id": "da3237bc-0adc-3025-8255-9611b3da52fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a tacit manner; done in silence or implied."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "43c855a7-5594-490e-adca-57cd6ceb4000",
                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                "text": "Your failure to object to the request resulted in you tacitly approving the change."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ba137f2-530d-429d-83ad-7e5063616ee7",
                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                "text": "The new accusation brought by Urban against Manfred of murdering his sister-in-law's embassador – it may be observed that, tacitly, he acquits him of parricide, fratricide, and nepoticide – requires a little explanation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e5592a0-2a44-454f-b309-ebdfb87bd8e1",
                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                "text": "Since old Waziri’s death Tarzan had been directing the warriors in battle, and the temporary command had been tacitly conceded to him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c9e3986-58da-4bc9-b586-610c8ef0621c",
                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                "text": "The assumption that these are identical in meaning and usage between Indian English and Anglo-American English, while tacitly accepted, is untested, and fundamentally unknown."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5cc2ec04-1d8e-4076-b64a-03a97f5a6722",
                                "sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                                "text": "Regarding the “3.5% rule”, she [Erica Chenoweth] points out that while 3.5% is a small minority, such a level of active participation probably means many more people tacitly agree with the cause."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d31c1197-6427-4c70-b1ec-ed2359cf5028",
                        "source_entry_id": "da3237bc-0adc-3025-8255-9611b3da52fb",
                        "source_sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
                        "source_sense_description": "in a tacit manner",
                        "target_lang_word": "tacitement",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tacitement",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03123fb5-993f-3bf0-8a68-d30148fa13d4",
                                        "entry_id": "ae076d72-f647-307e-b61a-291cf4e2ae0e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "D’une manière tacite, sans être formellement exprimé."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df4603ed-41a2-47a7-a14e-5b3cf158f1ee",
                                                "sense_id": "03123fb5-993f-3bf0-8a68-d30148fa13d4",
                                                "text": "Les ennemis de Lamotte l’ont accusé d’avoir ambitionné la monarchie universelle en littérature ; peut-être aspirait-il tacitement à cette gloire, sans trop s'en douter,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76285917-36a1-4af3-8915-38efa8786de2",
                                                "sense_id": "03123fb5-993f-3bf0-8a68-d30148fa13d4",
                                                "text": "Cela n’est pas exprimé dans le traité, mais cela y est compris tacitement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bada42d-4e7a-4297-9bc9-0a5a509f0c09",
                                                "sense_id": "03123fb5-993f-3bf0-8a68-d30148fa13d4",
                                                "text": "Ce contrat est tacitement reconductible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2dc602af-d552-4ee0-b092-6c64b86fe31e",
                        "source_entry_id": "da3237bc-0adc-3025-8255-9611b3da52fb",
                        "source_sense_id": "f111e198-1621-353a-84e3-07362fcd7fd5",
